  "source_id": "county-031",
  "text": "Board of Elections | Duplin County, NC\nSkip to Main Content\nCreate a Website Account\n- Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nGovernment\nDepartments\nServices\nNews\nCommunity\nHow Do I...\nSearch\nBoard of Election Board Minutes\nHome\nGovernment\nCounty Boards, Committees & Commissions\nBoard of Elections\nBoard of Elections\nMeetings\n5:30 pm\n1st Thursday of every month\nElections Office\n160 Mallard Street\nKenansville, NC 28349\nPlease contact the Board of Elections office to confirm the monthly Board meeting schedule. Absentee Board meetings will begin every Tuesday starting on September 29 to November 3, 2026 at 5 pm.\nCall in number\n605-313-5759\nAccess Number: 5257917\nNotices\nLegal Notice\nAgendas & Minutes\nAgendas are available prior to the meetings. Minutes are available following approval.\nView Most Recent Agendas and Minutes\nMembers\nAnn Henderson, Chair\nAngela B. Mainor, Secretary\nBeverly Trobaugh, Member\nMichael Lynch, Member\nRoland Penny, Member\nStaff\nCarrie Sullivan, Director\nAnalaysia Davis, Deputy Director\nOverview\nNeed to find your polling place? Visit the NC Board of Elections\nPolling Place Search\n.\nView the\nPhoto ID Notice\n.\nMission Statement\nThe Mission of the Duplin County Board of Elections is to provide our services in the most efficient and timely manner. We strive to provide the highest level of professional standards to ensure accurate, honest, and fair elections for every citizen. It is our top priority to provide every citizen the opportunity to exercise their right to vote, which is the foundation of American Freedom.\nGeneral Services Provided\nThe Board of Elections is responsible for conducting all elections held in Duplin County. The Board administers and oversees all federal, state, and local elections. A few of our principal functions include:\nEstablishing election precincts and voting sites\nAppointing and training precinct officials\nDesigning, preparing, and distributing ballots\nProcuring, testing, and maintaining voting equipment\nCanvassing and certifying the ballots cast in elections\nInvestigating any voting irregularities\nMaintaining voter registration and participation records\nConducting candidate filing\nReceiving, auditing and maintaining campaign finance reports\nProviding public information upon request\nRelated Information\nUOCAVA Election Notice (PDF\n)\n2023 Voter ID Requirement Information Sheet (PDF)\n2026 Common ID Flyer (PDF)\nElected Officials Directory\nElection Districts Map/Precincts\nElection Notice (PDF)\nElection Results Dashboard on North Carolina State Board of Elections website\nNC Voter ID information\nVote by Mail\n2026 Election Calendar of Events\n2026 Early Voting Times and Location\n2026 General Election Absentee Request Form\nNot sure if you are registered to vote? Check here!\nVoter Search\nContact Us\nCarrie Sullivan\nDirector\nEmailCarrie Sullivan\nBoard of Elections\nEmail the Board of Elections\nPhysical Address\nView Map\n160 Mallard Street\nKenansville\n,\nNC\n28349\n160 Mallard Street Kenansville NC 28349\nDirections\nMailing Address\nP.O. Box 975\nKenansville\n,\nNC\n28349\nPhone:\n910-296-2170\nFax: 910-296-2167\nHours\nMonday through Friday\n8 am to 5 pm\nDirectory\nForms\nPrecinct Official Application (PDF)\nSolicitud de Inscripci\u00f3n para Votar (PDF)\nVoter Registration Application (PDF)\nPrecinct Buffer Zones\nAlbertson (PDF)\nBeulaville (PDF)\nCalypso (PDF)\nCedar Fork (PDF)\nCharity (PDF)\nChinquapin (PDF)\nCypress Creek (PDF)\nFaison (PDF)\nGlisson (PDF)\nHallsville (PDF)\nKenansville (PDF)\nMagnolia (PDF)\nRose Hill (PDF)\nSmith Cabin (PDF)\nWallace (PDF)\nWarsaw (PDF)\nWolfscrape (PDF)\nEmployment\nDuplin GIS Maps\nLegal Notices\nTax Foreclosures\nEvents Calendar\nOnline Payments\nContact Us\nDuplin County Administrative Office\n224 Seminary Street\nKenansville, NC 28349\nPhone:\n910-296-2104\nContact Us\nQuick Links\nPublic Records Request\nHoliday Calendar\nEmployees\nIntranet\nHelp Desk\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nSite Links\nHome\nSite Map\nContact Us\nAccessibility\nCopyright Notices\nPrivacy Policy\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nGovernment Websites by\nCivicPlus\u00ae\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\nArrow Left\nArrow Right\n[]\nSlideshow Left Arrow\nSlideshow Right Arrow",
